{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 complete — RED→GREEN, mutation-checked, held out\n\n**Test (RED first).** `tests/unit/metrics/test_lizard_complexity_heldout.py` and\n`tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py`. Three oracles, all observed failing for the\nright reason BEFORE any fix existed:\n\n- `test_empty_analysis_is_unavailable_not_a_confident_zero` — the corrected form of the old\n  `test_empty_analysis_has_zero_aggregates`, which asserted the defect.\n- `test_root_without_any_language_lizard_supports_is_unavailable` — the reported scenario\n  driven through the REAL library, not a fake.\n- `test_zero_scanned_sources_is_unavailable_not_a_confident_zero` (jscpd).\n\nPlus `test_measurable_root_never_reports_a_zero_complexity` (AC3), green before and after —\nit is a regression guard, not an oracle.\n\n**Held out.** The three RED tests were moved OUT of the working tree before the fix subagent\nwas launched; it was told `tests/` was off-limits and was given only the mechanism + the\ncontract. It never saw the assertions. They were restored afterwards and passed — GREEN\nagainst an oracle the fixer could not read.\n\n**Mutation check (teeth).** Re-seeding each defect exactly — deleting the `if not files`\nguard, and deleting the zero-`sources` raise — returns all three tests to RED; restoring the\nfix returns them to GREEN. Refactoring litmus: every assertion is on an observable return\nvalue (`Unavailable` vs `AnalyzerResult`), never a private name or a source grep.\n\n**Fix.** `lizard_complexity.analyze` returns `_unavailable(\"lizard reported no files\")` on an\nempty map, with the `_LOGGER` + `_unavailable` helper pair both sibling adapters already\ncarry. `run_jscpd` raises on an explicit zero `sources`, reusing the existing\n`ValueError` -> `Unavailable` conversion. +28 lines of non-test code, both mirroring\n`scc_loc`'s guard.\n\n**Fix-safety audit.** Restoration, not creation — no new entry point or capability, a wrong\nvalue corrected. No new dependency (`logging` is stdlib and already used by both sibling\nadapters). No test weakened — the one changed assertion is an expectation flip from the\nbuggy zero to `Unavailable`, which strengthens it.\n\n**Caller sweep — all THREE `run_jscpd` callers verified, not just the two the ticket named.**\n`jscpd_dup.analyze` converts `ValueError` to `Unavailable`; `git_metrics._structural_spec`\nalready branches on `Unavailable`; and `scripts/backfill_complexity_clone_snapshots.py`\nreaches `run_jscpd` via `_measure_clone_count`, which runs inside `measure_tree`'s\n`except (... ValueError ...)` and returns `None`. So the historical backfill now records \"no\nmeasurement\" instead of a fabricated zero — the same invariant, applied one layer out. No\ncaller depended on the zero.\n\n**Sibling sweep.** Construct axis: the tree contains exactly THREE `AnalyzerResult(`\nconstruction sites — `scc_loc` (guarded by c5b3), `lizard_complexity` and `jscpd_dup` (guarded\nhere). The class is closed, not bounded. Parity axis: the rule is \"a structural metric must not\npublish a zero it did not measure\"; the only channel is the metrics registry, and all three\nanalyzers now hold it.\n\n## Cross-change interaction found and verified — change 1487 / ticket 4bf4\n\nWhile running the suite I hit `test_live_clone` failing (`assert 0 >= 1`). Verified it fails\nIDENTICALLY on clean origin/main, so it is pre-existing, not a regression from this change. It\nis `@pytest.mark.integration` and CI never installs jscpd, so it always skipped there.\n\nIt is already being fixed independently by change 1487 (ticket 4bf4) — its fixture sat below\njscpd's default `--min-tokens 50` floor. That change touches the SAME FILE as this one, so I\nchecked both compatibility axes:\n\n- **Semantic — compatible, and mutually reinforcing.** 4bf4 adds a negative control asserting\n  `AnalyzerResult` with `clones == 0` for two DISTINCT files, documented as \"both files clear\n  the token floor, so a zero here means 'no duplication found', not 'nothing was examined'\" —\n  which is precisely the invariant this ticket enforces. Built its exact fixture and ran real\n  jscpd: `sources: 2, clones: 0`, so this guard correctly does NOT fire and its assertion holds.\n- **Textual — conflicts.** Both changes insert new functions at the same point in\n  `test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py`. Verified by cherry-picking 1487 onto this branch: one purely\n  additive conflict, trivially resolved by keeping both. With BOTH applied, all 12 tests in the\n  jscpd + lizard modules pass, INCLUDING the two integration tests that fail today.\n\nWhichever lands second rebases; the resolution is keep-both. Flagging so it is not rediscovered.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n`test_live_clone`'s skip guard checks only that jscpd is on PATH, not that it actually measured\nanything — which is how a below-floor fixture went unattributed since the day it was written.\nNot fixed here (it is 4bf4's ticket, and widening into it would repeat the scope mistake this\nticket exists to avoid). Recorded, not silently dropped."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786101963280990001,"uuid":"801fb4ea-528a-414d-a270-8b897532fb74"}